# aircraft-fleet: shared environment configuration
# Copy to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.sample .env
#
# One .env at the aircraft-fleet root is read by both projects:
#   - pipeline/: setup.sh and the populate_aircraft_db loader
#   - supervisor-agent/: the local server, and agent.sh for deploy
# Existing environment variables are never overridden, so shell-exported vars
# and the deployed AgentCore Runtime's injected env vars take precedence.

# =============================================================================
# Neo4j connection (required, shared by the pipeline and supervisor-agent/)
# =============================================================================
# The pipeline populates this instance. supervisor-agent/ connects to it
# directly with the Neo4j driver. Both MUST point at the same database, or
# vector search and Text2Cypher return nothing.

NEO4J_URI=neo4j+s://xxxxxxxx.databases.neo4j.io
NEO4J_USERNAME=neo4j
NEO4J_PASSWORD=your-password
NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j

# =============================================================================
# Agent memory (required by supervisor-agent/)
# =============================================================================
# The agent keeps conversation memory in a separate Neo4j database, not the
# fleet graph. The agent server stops at startup if the URI or the password is
# missing. Local runs default the username and database to neo4j. A deploy
# needs all four NEO4J_* and MEM_NEO4J_* connection settings set here, apart
# from the passwords.

MEM_NEO4J_URI=neo4j+s://yyyyyyyy.databases.neo4j.io
MEM_NEO4J_PASSWORD=your-memory-password
#MEM_NEO4J_USERNAME=neo4j
#MEM_NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j

# =============================================================================
# Deploy: Secrets Manager password ARNs (required for deploy only)
# =============================================================================
# `./agent.sh deploy` passes these to the AgentCore Runtime instead of the
# passwords. supervisor-agent/ needs both. The Runtime reads each login from
# its secret at startup.
# Each secret holds a JSON object with a `password` key and an optional
# `username` key, such as {"username": "fleet_reader", "password": "..."}.
# When the secret has a `username`, the agent uses it instead of
# NEO4J_USERNAME or MEM_NEO4J_USERNAME. So NEO4J_USERNAME above can stay the
# admin user the pipeline writes as, while the agent reads as a read-only
# user. Use the complete ARN, which ends in the six-character suffix that
# Secrets Manager adds. Set these before ./agent.sh deploy. Once they are
# set, local runs also read the passwords from Secrets Manager, so they need
# AWS credentials and connect as the secret's user. Export an empty value,
# such as NEO4J_PASSWORD_SECRET_ARN=, to use the passwords above instead.

#NEO4J_PASSWORD_SECRET_ARN=arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-east-1:123456789012:secret:fleet-neo4j-AbCdEf
#MEM_NEO4J_PASSWORD_SECRET_ARN=arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-east-1:123456789012:secret:fleet-memory-AbCdEf

# =============================================================================
# pipeline/: dataset size (default or full)
# =============================================================================
# false (default): 30 aircraft over 90 days. That is about 800,000 nodes and
#                  830,000 relationships, mostly hourly sensor readings.
#                  nodes_readings.csv is about 54 MB. It answers every query
#                  in supervisor-agent/fleet_supervisor/client/queries.txt.
# true:            100 aircraft over 90 days. That is about 2.7 million nodes,
#                  with about 180 MB of readings. It is slower to load.
# Both sizes are past the Aura Free limits of 200,000 nodes and 400,000
# relationships. Use a paid Aura tier or a local Neo4j.

LOAD_FULL_DATASET=false

# Optional fine-grained overrides (take precedence over LOAD_FULL_DATASET).
# Leave unset to use the size implied by LOAD_FULL_DATASET.
#GEN_AIRCRAFT=20
#GEN_DAYS=7
#GEN_AIRPORTS=40
#GEN_SEED=42

# =============================================================================
# pipeline/: GraphRAG enrichment LLM (required for `setup`)
# =============================================================================
# `setup` chunks the maintenance manuals in manuals/, embeds the chunks, and
# extracts entities. LLM_PROVIDER selects the backend for BOTH the embeddings
# and the entity-extraction LLM.
#
#   bedrock (default): Amazon Bedrock, with Titan Text Embeddings V2 and
#                      Claude. No API keys here. It uses the standard AWS
#                      credential chain: env vars, ~/.aws, or an instance role.
#   openai:            OpenAI embeddings and OpenAI extraction.
#   anthropic:         OpenAI embeddings and Anthropic extraction. Run
#                      `uv sync --extra anthropic` first.
#
# Run `./setup.sh load-operational` instead if you want CSV data only and no
# LLM calls (no keys / no AWS needed).

LLM_PROVIDER=bedrock

# ── Amazon Bedrock (used when LLM_PROVIDER=bedrock) ─────────────────────────
# AWS credentials come from the environment or ~/.aws. Do not put them here.
# The region is the shared AWS_REGION below, one setting for the pipeline and
# the agent. It defaults to us-east-1, this repo's AgentCore region.
#BEDROCK_LLM_MODEL=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5
#BEDROCK_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=8000
#BEDROCK_EMBEDDING_MODEL=amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0
#BEDROCK_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024

# ── OpenAI (used when LLM_PROVIDER=openai; embeddings when =anthropic) ──────
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here
#OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
#OPENAI_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1536
#OPENAI_EXTRACTION_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
#OPENAI_EXTRACTION_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS=8000

# ── Anthropic (used when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic) ───────────────────────────
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here
#ANTHROPIC_EXTRACTION_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
#ANTHROPIC_EXTRACTION_MAX_TOKENS=8000

# Chunking
#CHUNK_SIZE=800
#CHUNK_OVERLAP=100
#ENRICH_SAMPLE_SIZE=0
#SAMPLE_SIZE=10

# =============================================================================
# pipeline/: data locations (managed by setup.sh, do not normally edit)
# =============================================================================
# setup.sh exports DATA_DIR and DOCUMENT_DIR as absolute paths before running
# the loader, so the vendored tool finds generated CSVs and the manuals.
#DATA_DIR=
#DOCUMENT_DIR=

# =============================================================================
# AWS region + agent model (optional; defaults shown)
# =============================================================================
# AWS credentials come from the standard chain: env vars, ~/.aws, or an
# instance role. AWS_REGION is the single shared region: the pipeline uses it
# for Bedrock (when LLM_PROVIDER=bedrock) and the agent uses it for Bedrock
# and AgentCore. Defaults to us-east-1, this repo's AgentCore region.

#AWS_REGION=us-east-1
#MODEL_ID=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5

# =============================================================================
# supervisor-agent/: vector index and embedder (optional, MUST match pipeline)
# =============================================================================
# Override only if the pipeline ran with non-default embedding settings. The
# index name and dimensions must agree with how the graph was populated.

#VECTOR_INDEX_NAME=maintenanceChunkEmbeddings
#EMBED_MODEL_ID=amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0
#EMBED_DIMENSIONS=1024
